---
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../../consts";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description={`How ${SITE_TITLE} is built: framework, typography, design tokens, progressive enhancement and feeds.`}
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Colophon</h1>

  <div class="about-prose">
    <p>
      What this publication is built with, and what it deliberately leaves out.
    </p>

    <h2>Framework and output</h2>
    <p>
      Static HTML generated by Astro, with Markdown articles stored in this
      repository and validated against a schema at build time. Invalid
      frontmatter fails the build; drafts and future-dated articles are excluded
      from every public page, feed and index.
    </p>

    <h2>Typography</h2>
    <p>
      Headings use a serif system stack (Iowan Old Style, Palatino, Georgia and
      friends); body text and controls use the platform sans-serif stack; code
      and technical labels use a monospace stack (Cascadia Mono, Source Code
      Pro, Menlo and friends). No remote fonts are loaded, so text rendering
      never blocks on network requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Color and modes</h2>
    <p>
      Design tokens are defined once in <code>src/styles/tokens.css</code>: a
      warm paper canvas, near-black ink, a terracotta accent and a quiet sage.
      Light and dark palettes follow the system preference by default and can be
      switched with the theme control, which persists your choice.
    </p>

    <h2>Interaction</h2>
    <p>
      Client-side JavaScript is limited to small, progressive parts: the theme
      toggle, the mobile navigation menu, code copying on article pages, and
      this site's search. Every page stays readable and navigable with
      JavaScript disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics, no tracking, no third-party scripts, no accounts and no
      cookies. The only thing this site stores is your theme preference, kept in
      your browser's local storage and never sent anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Discovery</h2>
    <p>
      New articles are available as <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>, and the site
      publishes a sitemap for search engines. Editorial standards and the
      correction policy live on the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
